  "notes": [
    "Primary site: eddirasa.com. Its /bac-solutions/subject/<slug>/ pages list every BAC session 2008-2026 for one subject, each with a 'الموضوع' link and a 'التصحيح' link. A page covers ALL streams that sit that subject, grouped under stream labels (e.g. arabic/french/english: 'الشعب العلمية', 'آداب وفلسفة', 'لغات أجنبية'; physics: 'علوم تجريبية' and 'رياضيات وتقني رياضي'; philosophy: 'رياضيات وعلوم تجريبية', 'تسيير واقتصاد وتقني رياضي', 'آداب وفلسفة', 'لغات أجنبية'). The app should tell the student to scroll to their stream's section. 'level: subject' here means a subject page for every stream, not a page filtered to one stream; neither site has stream+subject pages.",
    "eddirasa per-year per-stream pages also exist, e.g. https://eddirasa.com/ens-sec/3as/bac-solutions/bac-2026/sciences/ (slugs: sciences, mathematics, technical-mathematics, management-economics, literature-philosophy, foreign-languages). Each covers one session only, so they were not used as stream-level links. They could serve as a 'latest session' shortcut.",
    "Fallback site: dzexams.pro (the old dzexams.com could not be fetched). Its subject pages /ar/bac?mod=<code> list 2008-2026 with a 'الحل' link per year (ministerial plus detailed solution, as the site describes it). WARNING: while checking, query-string URLs sometimes came back with the wrong subject: bac.php?mod=fr|eng|hist showed the physics page, bac?mod=hist showed Islamic studies, and one fetch of bac?mod=gestion showed Italian. Every dzexams URL kept here showed the right subject heading at least once. Even so, a periodic re-check is recommended, and dzexams should stay the fallback.",
    "Mixed URL forms on dzexams: the accounting, g-e, g-p, germany and italy entries use the bac.php?mod= form that was actually fetched. The site's canonical form is https://www.dzexams.pro/ar/bac?mod=<code> (gestion, g-e, g-p, germany, italy).",
    "Unverified, so left out: dzexams history-geography (https://www.dzexams.pro/ar/bac?mod=hist and bac.php?mod=hist both served a different subject); dzexams civil engineering (bac.php?mod=g-c served the BAC hub page); dzexams arts (bac.php?mod=dessin served the hub page; it is an arts-education section, not the BAC arts stream).",
    "Arts stream (شعبة فنون): neither eddirasa nor dzexams has an arts-stream section, and their subject pages carry no arts-stream label. a-onec.com has arts pages (https://www.a-onec.com/2026/06/bac-Arts.html, https://www.a-onec.com/2025/06/bac-Arts.html), but the subject table has no hrefs and actually shows 2024 labels, so nothing was linked. Only arts/islamic is filled (the Islamic sciences paper is labelled 'كل الشعب' / 'جميع الشعب'). All other arts subjects are empty arrays and need a source later.",
    "technology (تقني رياضي) and third_language (لغات أجنبية) have one entry per option, with an extra 'option_ar' field (engineering branch / language). eddirasa covers all 4 engineering branches and all 3 languages (Italian only from 2015). dzexams covers 3 engineering branches (no civil) and all 3 languages.",
    "The svt link for the math stream is correct: both sites' SVT pages have a 'شعبة رياضيات' section. Islamic sciences is one common paper for all streams on both sites.",
    "Other sites seen but not used: a-onec.com (one page per year and stream, e.g. https://www.a-onec.com/2024/06/bac-exam-sience.html, with correction links); bac-algerie.net (one page per stream with a PDF per session, e.g. https://bac-algerie.net/sujets-filiere-Sciences-experimentales.html; whether corrections are included was not confirmed); bac-feljib.com, touahria.com (physics only), dzdbac.com. The official ONEC site (bac.onec.dz / onec.dz) could not be reached and had no archive in search results.",
    "Amazigh (optional) and pe were skipped as instructed. For reference, eddirasa and dzexams both list Amazigh on their hubs (dzexams mod=amazigh); this was not verified.",
    "Copyright: only index pages are linked. No paper or solution content is copied."
  ]
}